WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.508
Permissions control which operations an account can perform.

00:00:03.508 --> 00:00:08.331
Authentication establishes an identity; authorisation decides what that identity may do.

00:00:08.331 --> 00:00:15.785
Least privilege means granting only the access necessary for a task and reviewing it when responsibilities change.

00:00:16.785 --> 00:00:21.173
The backend must reject the request when the session lacks teacher privileges.

00:00:21.173 --> 00:00:27.755
The interface is not a trusted enforcement boundary because a user can construct requests without using its buttons.

00:00:28.755 --> 00:00:30.298
What is authorisation?

00:00:30.298 --> 00:00:33.385
Authorisation checks permitted actions and resources.
